# --- secrets ---
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# --- python ---
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# --- data (large binaries never live in git; >5 MB goes to Hugging Face Datasets) ---
*.parquet
*.duckdb
data/
# Date-stamped scraper dumps. Local working copies only; the published archive goes to HF Datasets.
archives/
# Frozen vintage exports (scripts/export_vintage.py). 12 MB for the 2026-11-16 vintage, so above the
# 5 MB git rule; the published copy belongs on Hugging Face Datasets, not in the repo.
vintage/

# --- build output ---
# The public page and its JSON are generated from the database by scripts/build_site.py and published
# by the `publish` job in .github/workflows/daily.yml. Build output, never source: a stale copy in git
# would be a page nobody re-derived.
site/

# --- run logs ---
# Local scraper/flow stdout capture. Evidence worth keeping goes into PROGRESS.md, not here.
*.log

# --- agent tickets (see ~/.config/opencode/runtime/README.md) ---
# Briefs and progress are working notes. Reports are kept: they are what was actually verified.
.agent/*-brief.md
.agent/*-progress.md

# --- os / editor ---
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.idea/
.vscode/
.neon
# Playwright MCP writes screenshots and accessibility snapshots here during UI checks.
.playwright-mcp/

# A superseded manual eyeball sheet, kept on disk for provenance and never to be used. Tracked here
# so the working tree stays clean: its replacement is the verification desk.
.agent/eyeball-sheet.md

# --- agent scratch (21 Nov 2026) ---
# Screenshots, build logs, generated copies and replay patches are working material: the reports are the
# record, and the images a reader needs live in docs/readme. Two patch scripts that PROGRESS.md names as
# replayable are committed deliberately, so the ignore rules below are by pattern, not by folder.
.agent/*.png
.agent/*-shots/
.agent/*.txt
.agent/_*.py
.agent/T1120-c-head.py
.agent/T1120-c-broken.py
.agent/T1120-c-about-good.html
.agent/recover/build_site.*.py
